{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AyUvpnnjjdnoZyktpnnKKc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019kZeUtNyUrR1ChcNSytNDb","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a8983623d9f2944d8","message":"## Step 2: Cross-Review Exchange\n\nHere is Reviewer 2's review. Read it carefully, then provide:\n1. Points of agreement with R2\n2. Points of disagreement with R2\n3. Whether R2's observations change your assessment\n4. Any revised or additional concerns\n5. Your final score (may stay the same or change)\n\n---\n\n## R2 Review: Novelty, Positioning, and Related Work\n\n### Summary\nThis paper evaluates whether hidden-state probes for safety commitment detection in reasoning models generalize across model scale, using a 2x2 matrix of architectures and scales. The central finding is negative: the hidden-state monitoring advantage observed at 7-8B parameters vanishes at 32B, with Fisher discriminability dropping 6x and all recovery strategies failing. The paper positions this as a cautionary result for the deployment of probe-based safety monitors on production-scale reasoning systems.\n\n### Strengths\n- S1: Research question is timely and practically important\n- S2: 2x2 experimental design with OpenThinker-7B is well-constructed\n- S3: Thoroughness of negative evidence is commendable (systematic elimination of alternatives)\n- S4: Fisher discriminability provides clean interpretable summary\n- S5: Statistical methodology is reasonable (bootstrap CIs, AUROC, p-values)\n\n### Weaknesses\n- W1: **Confounded experimental design** — all 32B models are Qwen2.5 distillations from same teacher. Could be \"distillation-into-Qwen2.5-32B effect\" not a scale effect. Missing Llama-32B cell.\n- W2: **Related Work inadequate** — ~0.5 pages, ~14 citations. Missing: probing at scale literature, superposition hypothesis (Elhage et al.), mechanistic interpretability, concurrent reasoning safety work. Far below top venue density (40-60 refs).\n- W3: **No figures in 10 pages with 15 tables** — poor information design. Reads like experiment log, not persuasive narrative.\n- W4: **Overclaiming about production systems** — extrapolation from 32B distilled to 70B+ natively-trained is unsupported.\n- W5: **No theoretical framework** — superposition hypothesis would explain findings but isn't cited.\n- W6: **n=43 too small** — CIs include chance, so paper can't establish HS probes work at all at 32B.\n- W7: **Misleading framing** — ALL monitoring fails at 32B (AUROC ~0.57-0.60 for everything). The real finding is \"detection itself fails at scale\" not just \"HS advantage vanishes.\"\n\n### Score: 3/6 | Confidence: 4/5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9910,"cache_read_input_tokens":64918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9910},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5feb2154-bbc5-4d7e-891f-e50eada4cb93","uuid":"359ecbe0-7133-497d-aae6-cd0d3638c942"}
